(Ord. 08-201 § 1 (part), 2008)

333:
The installation and alteration of alarm systems shall be in accordance with Article 760 "Fire Protective Signaling Systems" of the National Electrical Code, NFPA Number 70-1975 and the following NFPA standards:
A. Standard 71 - Standard for the installation, maintenance, and use of central station signaling systems;
B. Standard 72-B - Standard for the installation, maintenance and use of auxiliary protective signaling systems for fire alarm service;
C. Standard 72-C - Standard for the installation, maintenance, and use of remote station protective signaling system;
D. Standards 72-D - Standard for the installation, maintenance, and use of remote station protective signaling systems for watchman, fire alarm and supervisory service;
E. Standards 72-E - Standard on automatic fire detectors;
F. Standard 74 - Standard for the installation, maintenance and use of household fire warning equipment.
(Ord. 98-4 (part), 1998)

335:
A. Request for Review. The alarm systems coordinator shall, when requested by an alarm user, review the determination that an alarm was false. Such review shall be conducted by the alarm systems coordinator only if the alarm user requests in writing such a review within ten (10) days of the date the alarm user was notified of the false alarm determination. The written request for review of a false alarm determination by the alarm systems coordinator shall include the following information:
A. Alarm user name;
B. Address at which alarm is installed;
C. Date of false alarm that is being contested; and
D. Facts upon which the request for review of the false alarm determination is made.
(Ord. 98-4 (part), 1998)

